<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jakob Sprenger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1884–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jakob Sprenger was a Nazi politician who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauleiter">Gauleiter</a> of Hesse-Nassau and, from 1933, as Reich governor of the People's State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. He oversaw the Nazi takeover of the state's government and the persecution of its Jewish communities, among them the old communities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and Worms. He killed himself at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jakob-sprenger.jpg" alt="Jakob Sprenger" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sprenger-jakob-das-deutsche-ledermuseum-zum-25jaehrigen-Jubilaeum-im-kriegsjahr_1942-offenbach-graphische-werkstaette-rudolph-1942-vorsatz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
